---
title: Style guide
description: The design system of the Scheldt Youth Parliament website, for checking the build against the design.
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
type: raw
lightbox: true
noindex: true
# The map in "One river, three countries" below uses the same data as About: src/_data/countriesMap.js.
# Do not put a countriesMap in this front matter: Eleventy would merge it with that file and draw the borders twice.
---
<section class="container page-hero">
  <div class="eyebrow">Style guide</div>
  <h1>The design system in code</h1>
  <p class="lead measure">This page shows every building block of the site, in GoodPlanet's house style. It is not linked from the menu. Use it to check colours, type, buttons, waves, cards and the river timeline.</p>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-bottom: var(--section)">
  <div class="split">
    <h2>Palette</h2>
    <div>
      <div class="sg-swatches">
        <div class="sg-swatch"><div class="sg-swatch-color" style="background:#1895D3"></div><strong>GoodPlanet blue</strong><span>#1895D3</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><div class="sg-swatch-color" style="background:#1376A7"></div><strong>Blue, for headings, text and surfaces</strong><span>#1376A7</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><div class="sg-swatch-color" style="background:#0D5173"></div><strong>Blue, hover</strong><span>#0D5173</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><div class="sg-swatch-color" style="background:#494132"></div><strong>Dark brown-grey</strong><span>#494132</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><div class="sg-swatch-color" style="background:#2E2B26"></div><strong>Ink</strong><span>#2E2B26</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><div class="sg-swatch-color" style="background:#675F55"></div><strong>Grey text</strong><span>#675F55</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><div class="sg-swatch-color" style="background:#D1EAF6"></div><strong>Mist</strong><span>#D1EAF6</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><div class="sg-swatch-color" style="background:#EDF7FB"></div><strong>Foam</strong><span>#EDF7FB</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><div class="sg-swatch-color" style="background:#AFCA14"></div><strong>Lime</strong><span>#AFCA14</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><div class="sg-swatch-color" style="background:#E9860D"></div><strong>Orange</strong><span>#E9860D</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><div class="sg-swatch-color" style="background:#E72D52"></div><strong>Pink</strong><span>#E72D52</span></div>
        <div class="sg-swatch"><div class="sg-swatch-color" style="background:#29AF8A"></div><strong>Green</strong><span>#29AF8A</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="sg-note" style="margin-top:20px">GoodPlanet's house style (Huisstijlgids 2025). GoodPlanet blue for waves, rivers, dots and large numbers; its darker variant #1376A7 for headings, links and buttons. The dark brown-grey #494132 marks the first label of Then and now. The four other secondary colours are accents only: the bars under the key figures and on the reasons to join, and the line icons.</p>
      <p class="sg-note">One adjustment for accessibility: GoodPlanet blue #1895D3 on white has a contrast of 3.3 to 1, enough for large text and shapes but too low for small text. Links, labels, buttons and the blue surfaces with white text use a darker GoodPlanet blue, #1376A7 (5.0 to 1). The secondary colours are too light for any text.</p>
      <table class="sg-table">
        <tr><th>Combination</th><th>Contrast</th><th>Result</th></tr>
        <tr><td>Ink on white</td><td>14.1 to 1</td><td>Passes</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Headings on white</td><td>5.0 to 1</td><td>Passes</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Grey text on white</td><td>6.3 to 1</td><td>Passes</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Grey text on Foam</td><td>5.8 to 1</td><td>Passes</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Blue for text on white</td><td>5.0 to 1</td><td>Passes</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Blue for text on Foam</td><td>4.6 to 1</td><td>Passes</td></tr>
        <tr><td>White on blue surfaces (footer, cards, key figures)</td><td>5.0 to 1</td><td>Passes</td></tr>
        <tr><td>GoodPlanet blue #1895D3 on white</td><td>3.3 to 1</td><td>Large text and shapes only</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Lime, orange, pink, green on white</td><td>1.9 to 4.3 to 1</td><td>Shapes only, never text</td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-bottom: var(--section)">
  <div class="split">
    <h2>Type</h2>
    <div class="stack">
      <div>
        <h1 style="font-size: var(--fs-h1)">Young people, one river, three countries.</h1>
        <p class="sg-note" style="margin-top:12px">Lato Bold, homepage title, 64 px on desktop and 38 px on a phone. Other pages use 58 to 36 px.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2>What is the SYP?</h2>
        <p class="sg-note" style="margin-top:12px">Lato Bold, section title, 42 to 30 px.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>The river so far</h3>
        <p class="sg-note" style="margin-top:12px">Lato Bold, small title, 24 to 20 px.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="lead measure">Lato Regular for the lead paragraph, 21 to 18 px. You explore the Scheldt with people your age from three countries, meet the ones who manage it, and hand your recommendations to the International Scheldt Commission.</p>
        <p class="article">Lato Regular for article text, 20 to 17 px, line height 1.6. Ghent knows what water does when it rises. We started with the question the city asks itself every winter: how do you keep a city dry without walling off its rivers?</p>
        <p class="text-grey" style="font-size: var(--fs-small)">Grey text, 15 px, for captions and secondary lines.</p>
        <p><span class="label">Label, 14 px, Water for text</span></p>
        <p><span class="todo">[TODO] notes look like this, in monospace, until the real content arrives</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="pull-quote"><p>The river does not stop at the border, and neither do its problems.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-bottom: var(--section)">
  <div class="split">
    <h2>Spacing and shapes</h2>
    <div class="stack">
      <p class="sg-note">8 px grid. Content width 1200 px. Section padding 112 px on desktop, 64 px on a phone. Text columns stay under 60 characters. Pill buttons. Photos and cards get 20 to 28 px corners. One wave shape, used as a section divider and as the river timeline, nowhere else.</p>
      <div class="sg-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#">Join the next group</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="#">See what we did</a>
        <a class="btn btn-accent" href="#">Youth voices</a>
        <a class="btn btn-small" href="#">See the full timeline</a>
        <div class="sg-shape"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="sg-row">
        <a class="link-arrow" href="#">About the project</a>
        <a class="link-back" href="#" style="margin:0">All exchanges</a>
      </div>
      {% waveMark %}
      <p class="sg-note">Double wave marks, centred above and below quotes, like the two strokes of a quotation mark; the one below is mirrored. Keyboard focus shows a 3 px Water outline, press Tab to see it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container" style="padding-bottom: var(--section-sm)">
  <div class="split">
    <h2>Waves and the blue band</h2>
    <p class="sg-note">The wave divider fills the colour of the section that follows. Below, the band with key figures, as on the Exchanges page and The Scheldt, each with a bar in one of GoodPlanet's secondary colours. The homepage band shows why to join instead (src/_data/whyJoin.json).</p>
  </div>
</section>
{% wave "var(--deep)" %}
<section class="figures">
  <div class="container figures-grid">
    <div><div class="figure-number">40</div><div class="figure-label">participants</div></div>
    <div><div class="figure-number">9</div><div class="figure-label">nationalities</div></div>
    <div><div class="figure-number">4</div><div class="figure-label">cross-border exchanges</div></div>
    <div><div class="figure-number">2012</div><div class="figure-label">observer at the International Scheldt Commission since</div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container section">
  <div class="split" style="margin-bottom: var(--block)">
    <h2>Cards</h2>
    <p class="sg-note">Four card styles: the small timeline card, the soft Foam card for recommendations, the outlined quote card and the dark call to action.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card-grid" style="margin-bottom: var(--block)">
    <div>
      <div class="mini-card" style="max-width:234px"><div class="river-date">May 2026</div><div class="mini-card-title">Ghent, Belgium</div><div class="mini-card-text">Exchange 4, floods and a letter to policymakers.</div></div>
      <div class="mini-card is-upcoming" style="max-width:234px;margin-top:12px"><div class="mini-card-title">Your turn next</div><div class="mini-card-text">A new group of 16 to 26 year olds.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-soft">
      <span class="label">Group 1</span>
      <h3>[TODO theme]</h3>
      <ul class="card-list">
        <li>[TODO] First recommendation of this group.</li>
        <li>[TODO] Second recommendation of this group.</li>
        <li>[TODO] Third recommendation of this group.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <blockquote class="card-quote">
      {% waveMark "sm" %}
      <p>[TODO] One sentence from a participant, taken from the reports, goes here.</p>
      {% waveMark "sm", "end" %}
      <cite>First name, France</cite>
    </blockquote>
  </div>
  <div class="card-dark">
    <div>
      <h2>Read the letter to policymakers</h2>
      <p>The full letter and the recommendations of the three groups, as we presented them to the International Scheldt Commission.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="btn btn-accent" href="#">Youth voices</a>
  </div>
</section>

