{# The map for "One river, three countries" on the About page (Tine chose option A on choice page 63, a soft band per country).
   Same data as on About, in src/_data/countriesMap.js; drawn by lib/scheldt-map.js, styles .countries-map-* in site.css. #}
<section class="container section-sm" id="countries-map">
  <div class="split">
    <h2>One river, three countries</h2>
    <div>
      {% scheldtCountries countriesMap %}
      <p class="sg-note" style="margin-top:16px">{% raw %}{% scheldtCountries countriesMap %}{% endraw %}, with countriesMap from src/_data/countriesMap.js: a soft band per country behind the river, split where the river crosses a border, and what the river is called in each country. Up to 420 px wide, the full column up to 360 px on phones; the smallest text stays 12 px on a 375 px phone. The tints and their contrast ratios are in site.css.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# The photo ribbon for About (Tine, file 63, option A, October 2026): shown here inside a text column, as on About,
